{
  "version": "demo-3",
  "note": "Deterministic safety rules in Finnish, Swedish and English. Texts are normalised before matching (lower case, ä→a, ö→o, å→a, punctuation removed; the apostrophe is kept, so a curly apostrophe becomes a space). The rules are intentionally cautious: negations are not interpreted. A demo policy that requires clinical validation.",
  "phraseRules": [
    {
